  "family": "Fabaceae",
  "memo": "This tree is known for its dense, dark green foliage and striking, smooth bark. It features elongated, oval leaves that provide ample shade, making it a popular choice for urban landscaping. In the spring, it produces small, creamy yellow flowers that add a subtle touch of color. Its wood is highly valued for its durability and attractive grain, often used in furniture making. This tree adapts well to a variety of soil types and requires minimal maintenance, thriving in both full sun and partial shade. Its robust nature and aesthetic appeal make it a versatile addition to parks and streetscapes.",
