  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree has elongated, dark green leaves that can be used to teach about leaf structure and function. It produces small, creamy-yellow flowers that offer a chance to discuss pollination and the role of flowers in plant reproduction. The wood is dense and durable, making it a good example for lessons on different types of timber and their uses. Its ability to thrive in various soil types can be explored in discussions about plant adaptability and soil science.",
